% The work the default planner does on the chain of stats-semi-naive.dl.
% The recursive rule reads edge, which is complete when the path component
% is planned, before path, which is still being derived: it scans the edges
% and looks up the paths ending where each edge begins.  The lookups read
% only matching tuples, and because a path inserted early in a round is seen
% by the lookups after it, the chain is closed in the first round and the
% second finds nothing new.

edge(a, b).
edge(b, c).
edge(c, d).
edge(d, e).
edge(e, f).
edge(f, g).

path(X, Y) :- edge(X, Y).
path(X, Z) :- path(X, Y), edge(Y, Z).

path(a, X)?
